OpenProject on FenrirOS
=======================

OpenProject lives in /opt/openproject (as upstream's packages), with its gems
in vendor/bundle; it runs on Ruby 4.0 (the ruby4.0 package, beside the system
ruby 3.4). Commands run through /usr/lib/openproject/run, which puts Ruby 4.0
first in PATH and loads /etc/openproject/env. Three dinit services, none
enabled: openproject-web (Puma, localhost:8080), openproject-worker (GoodJob)
and openproject-hocuspocus (collaborative editing, port 1234, optional).
Nothing is set up for you: no database, no site, no secret.

Needs PostgreSQL (13 or newer). memcached is optional (a cache; without it
the cache is files under /opt/openproject/tmp). Optional tools OpenProject
uses when present: pdftotext (poppler), tesseract (text of attachments, for
search), git/subversion (repositories).

1. PostgreSQL: a role and a database:
     createuser -P openproject; createdb -O openproject openproject
2. cp /usr/share/doc/openproject/env.example /etc/openproject/env
   (chown root:openproject, chmod 0640) and fill in DATABASE_URL,
   SECRET_KEY_BASE (openssl rand -hex 64), OPENPROJECT_HOST__NAME and
   OPENPROJECT_HTTPS; memcached and Hocuspocus settings if wanted.
3. As openproject: /usr/lib/openproject/run bundle exec rake db:migrate db:seed
   The seed creates OpenProject's own first administrator, login "admin",
   password "admin", which it makes you change at the first login (set
   OPENPROJECT_SEED__ADMIN__USER__PASSWORD in the env file before seeding
   for another one).
4. nginx: /usr/share/doc/openproject/nginx-openproject.conf (an example);
   enable nginx, openproject-web and openproject-worker
   (dinitctl enable openproject-web ...), and openproject-hocuspocus with
   SECRET (and the same secret in OPENPROJECT_COLLABORATIVE__EDITING__HOCUSPOCUS__SECRET)
   if you want collaborative editing.

Attachments are kept in /var/lib/openproject/files
(OPENPROJECT_ATTACHMENTS__STORAGE__PATH). After an upgrade of the package,
run step 3's db:migrate again before restarting the services.

Not included: the BIM edition's model converters (IfcConvert,
COLLADA2GLTF, xeokit-metadata), which upstream downloads as prebuilt
binaries; the default ("standard") edition does not use them.
